===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|ram}}, {{m|gmh|rame||column, frame|g=f}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|rama||support|g=f}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*ramō||prop, frame}}, probably from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*rem(w)-||to rest, prop up; a support, base}}. Cognate with {{cog|gml|rame|rāme|g=m}}, {{cog|dum|rame|rāme|g=m}}, {{cog|nl|raam|g=n}}. Related to {{cog|de|Rand||edge|g=m}} and {{cog|de|Ranft||crust of bread|g=m}} (see also {{cog|de|Kanten}}), {{cog|goh|ramft}}, {{cog|gmh|ranft}}, {{m|gmh|ramft||edge, edging}}, {{cog|got|𐍂𐌹𐌼𐌹𐍃||silence}}, {{cog|sa|रमते||he sets at rest|tr=rámate}}, {{m|sa|रम्भ||prop, staff, support|tr=rambhá}}.

